--- /dev/null
+++ b/demos/era_advance.dem
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# era_advance.dem — Story 6.1's named golden: the S6 Era FSM advance
+# (Email → Streaming). The run starts in era 2 (the email-only era — the
+# director spawns email from the residentials; streaming is LOCKED by the era
+# roster). At tick 501 (25000ms) an advance to era 3 is REQUESTED (a LOGGED
+# Cmd_Era_Advance — the replay re-applies it from the blessed log, so the era
+# flip is replay-deterministic by construction, E10). No crisis is active, so
+# the E14 gate passes and era_step fires the advance the same tick: the era
+# byte flips, the Era_Advanced event emits, and the new era's unlocks load —
+# streaming becomes available (era 3 rosters it) and the demand signature
+# switches: era 3's demand (email res→res + streaming content_host→res) spawns
+# from the NEXT tick. The T1 pins the era-advanced state; the captures prove
+# the traffic visibly changes (pre-advance: email circles only; post-advance:
+# streaming triangles join the map — "the internet evolves, new traffic
+# appears"). The base draw (res→router→host over standard) gives the era-2
+# email spec a sink set (fixture qos adds two more residentials).
+seed 20261
+run 60000ms
+era 2
+fixture qos
+at 0ms draw 0 1 standard
+at 0ms draw 1 2 standard
+at 25000ms advance 3
+capture at 10000ms
+capture at 55000ms
